    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Annabelle Triabell is a leading Toreador on Chicago's primogen council. Though not a particularly potent political force in her own right, hers was the deciding vote that split the council against Prince Lodin in early 1983, sparking the Council Wars. She secretly groomed and supported the anarch leader Maldavis, receiving unknowing backing from both Critias and Helena, each of whom believed they alone were pulling her strings &mdash; when in truth Menele orchestrated the entire affair. She remains a quietly influential and dangerously underestimated player.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Let others underestimate you; smile pleasantly while you calculate three moves ahead. You enjoy being the one nobody suspects.</p>",
    "notes": "Deciding vote in the Council Wars. Secretly manipulated Maldavis's anarch uprising while believing herself an independent actor; unknowingly a pawn of Menele.",
